            <ArticleTitle>Migraine-related stroke in the context of the International Headache Society classification of head pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>458-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The diagnosis of migraine-related stroke is reviewed and illustrative case histories are provided. The International Headache Society classification of &quot;migrainous cerebral infarction&quot; is amplified and further categorized using strictly defined diagnostic criteria. True migraine-induced stroke is revealed as only one of a number of migraine-related stroke syndromes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
